{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "native_probe_makearray_in_multi_index_faq",
    "description": "A rank-1 makearray, read through `index` inside an faq over TWO output indices, whose region values read the other index: m[k,i] = [a[k], 2*u[k,2], c][i] (regions [1,1], [2,3], then [3,3] overwriting). The makearray is a per-cell array, so it has no whole-array lowering in the (k, i) box; native assembles it over the output box instead (EarthSciAST #709). Also read at a shifted subscript (n[k,i] = makearray[i+1] for i in [1,2]) and at a constant one (p[k,i] = makearray[2]). Further reads: q, with an empty region and a region no subscript reaches; r, a rank-2 makearray read inside a rank-1 faq; s and w, a same-rank makearray at permuted (s[k,i] = m2[i,k]) and shifted (w[k,i] = m2[k,i+1]) subscripts; x, makearrays under elementwise operations (2*m+1 and an ifelse choosing between two); y, all-literal values; z, a bounding box starting past 1, which the read indexes 1-based.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "native",
      "probe"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    },
    "ion": {
